EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Sundered_Eagle_TheIslands_AeliophanesOfHouseFlambeau" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Aeliophanes of House Flambeau"
    VERSION "0.5.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # Aeliophanes of House Flambeau (Chapter Six: The Islands, p85): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t6027c03887fb69b2eb4017 ^"Aeliophanes of House Flambeau" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t99d78701a695218b339395 ^"Favonius"]
            ^"Age" STRING "32 (Apparent Age: 19)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Adventurous +2, Proud +2, Careful –3"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 85
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Aeliophanes has his sanctum on *The Tereus*, but he spends little time there. He spends the majority of his hours on his personal vessel, a one-man sailing boat commissioned at his own expense from Memnos. He is a monster hunter, delighting in chasing down creatures purely for their vis. It is well-known in the Tribunal that if a covenant has a problem with a monster with which the magi cannot themselves cope, Aeliophanes will dispatch it for them — if he can be found to ask. His motivation is a lust for glory rather than a desire to help. But despite this, Aeliophanes is a likeable person and a favorite among the grogs thanks to his gung-ho attitude and Gentle Gift.\n\nAeliophanes appears to be in the prime of his life (he has the Unaging Virtue); a dark-haired young hero with a neatly trimmed beard. His spear is his talisman, and it is enchanted with several effects to enhance its use as a weapon without being stopped by the Might of the creatures he hunts."
    }

}
